{
  "sheet": "skills",
  "about": "One row per skill (4 per hero). slot: primary=M1 gun, secondary=M2 (Deadlock ability 1), utility=Shift (ability 2), ult=R (Deadlock ultimate in RoR2's special slot, locked until its charge meter fills). RoR2 survivors have 4 skills, so each hero has exactly these 4. Numbers are RoR2-scale: damagePct is % of the body's damage stat (RoR2 convention), cooldowns are RoR2 seconds. deadlock* columns hold the source values read from the player's Deadlock scripts/abilities.vdata (ClientVersion 6774) so every conversion is traceable. kind picks the generic EntityState that implements the row. Unused numeric params are 0, unused refs are \"none\" (filled on purpose, not missing). Balance targets: sustained primary DPS 300-450 %/s (Commando Double Tap ~ 400 %/s incl. downtime); secondaries 2-8 s; utilities 4-10 s; specials 8-14 s; ultimates 1500-3000 % total, gated by ultCharge. minDuration: hold skills (Flame Dash, the Seismic Impact hover) last at least this long on a tap and at most duration while held; 0 otherwise. vfx: our own Unity-built visual for the skill (an effects row of kind custom), or none. extra: a second RoR2 object the kind spawns (the Warbanner ward of Thunderhead), or none. expect: what the skill must measurably do, checked in test mode (enemy_damage, enemy_stun, enemy_burn, enemy_debuff:<buff>, self_buff:<buff>, self_heal, self_move, self_cloak).",
